- op: discuss  # 827a
  at: '2026-04-19T02:04:39Z'  # 827a
  by: agent  # 827a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 827a
  clock: 8  # 827a
  nonce: 827a  # 827a
  message: "Plain-language recap: rather than change how ~35 language analyzers build their IDs, I added a single normalization pass in run_behavior_map that runs once after analysis completes. The pass walks every Symbol, Edge, and UsageContext and strips the absolute repo-root-plus-slash prefix from every id, path, src, and dst. So python:/home/me/repo/src/main.py:1-10:foo:function becomes python:src/main.py:1-10:foo:function. All repo-root knowledge lives in cli.py where repo_root is already a resolved Path, so no analyzer needs a new parameter. Subtlety: UsageContext.id is a sha256 that includes the path in its preimage, so the helper recomputes the id from the relativized path too — otherwise two machines would produce different usage-context ids for the same code. Comprehensiveness across all hypergumbo-supported languages: YES, and that's why I picked post-analysis over per-analyzer. The rewrite is language-agnostic string processing on whatever IDs the analyzers emit (python, go, rust, java, kotlin, svelte, wgsl, mermaid, etc.) — any future analyzer emitting {lang}:{absolute_path}:... gets relativized for free. Tests pin two non-trivial edge cases: (1) paths outside repo_root (external-library symbols) are deliberately left alone; (2) synthetic non-path IDs like python:external:0-0:foo:unresolved survive unchanged because the prefix never appears in them. Limitation: rewrite affects only the final behavior-map JSON and its readers. In-process IR objects carry absolute paths up to the relativization point; after the helper runs, ranking, entrypoint detection, handler-slice emission, and JSON write all see the relative form. Linker-internal data structures built earlier are absolute-path-based but never persist across runs. (Note: this reply was posted earlier tonight but lost by auto-pr's rebase-restore of .ops backups — WI-buhov hazard; re-posting verbatim.)"  # 827a
